  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "A", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    One owner, one purse, one signature: the sole proprietorship.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "B", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    There is no separate legal person, so personal property is available to creditors.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "A", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    The single owner takes every naira of profit, which is the form's strongest incentive.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "C", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    The business ends with the owner, so there is no perpetual succession.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "C", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Two to twenty; a larger firm must incorporate.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "C", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    The partnership deed sets capital, profit ratio, salaries and succession.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "A", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    The default rule shares profits and losses equally, whatever the capital.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "B", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Inactivity does not limit liability, which is why a sleeping partner is not a limited partner.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "A", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    The limited partner risks only what he put in, and may not bind the firm.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "B", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    He lends standing rather than money, and remains fully liable.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "D", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Held out to the world as a partner, he is liable as one.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "A", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    The creditor may recover the whole from one partner, who then recovers from the others.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "D", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Members own and control it, usually on the basis of one member one vote.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "A", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    The dividend reflects how much a member traded with the society.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "B", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Control follows membership, not the size of the shareholding.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "D", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    It buys in bulk and passes the saving to members.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "B", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Marketing cooperatives handle members' produce and share the proceeds.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "D", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Members save together and borrow from the pool.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "A", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Company votes follow shares; cooperative votes follow membership.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "A", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Profit is a means; the purpose is the members' economic need.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "C", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Creditors may reach beyond the business to the owner's own property.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "B", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    A partnership brings in capital and skill without incorporation.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "C", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    The deed governs capital, profit, salaries, interest and succession.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "C", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Tax rates are set by statute, not by the partners.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "A", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    The deed can provide for continuation, which is why it should be written.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "C", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    The member risks what he has subscribed and no more.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "A", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Cooperatives register under cooperative law, not as companies.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "B", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    There is no incorporation, so no separate legal personality.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "B", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    A limited partnership needs at least one partner with unlimited liability.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "C", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    More owners mean more capital and more combined skill.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "B", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Shared control is the price of shared capital.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "C", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Partners contribute capital, and may also lend to the firm.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "B", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Trading with non-members is allowed; the surplus still belongs to members.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "A", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    A cooperative continues as members come and go, unlike the other two.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "C", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Two or more professionals can pool skill, clients and costs.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "D", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    The nominal partner's contribution is standing, and his liability is unlimited.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "B", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Without incorporation there is no legal separation between owner and business.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "B", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Nearly every comparison question in the chapter reduces to those three.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "C", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    Democratic control and service to members are its defining features.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "D", dense: true, pad: 19.69pt)[
    The cooperative member risks only his shares; the sole trader risks everything.
  ]

]

